                  <msItem>
                     <title>Petrus Lombardus, Commentarius in Psalmos</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Binding of red velvet, faded to brown, over
                        boards: 2 metal clasps (1 now lost, the 2nd incomplete); metal corner
                        pieces, and 5 flat bosses on each cover; label formerly on front cover
                        (framents of green silk and nails used for securing the binding remain).
                        This is a binding made for Henry VIII (cf. Queen's Coll. 317, 323; Bodl.
                        Auct D.1.15). Title "Augustinus super Psalterium" at head of fol. 1r,
                        probably in Leland's hand. Inscription above this, probably "Liber
                        monasterii eveshamie", erased.</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate when-custom="13XX">s. xiv</origDate>
                  </origin>
